  "evidenceBoundary": "conditional: common ECS shape setup computes configuration from its secondary option, geometry kind and actor/body mode. This proves native branches and typed getters, not execution of a selected branch, current runtime flags, filter-shader selection, contact generation or solver participation.",
  "representation": {
    "secondaryOption": "A true incoming secondary option clears simulation, enables scene query, and selects trigger versus query-only using a separately read runtime setting. Stored secondaryFlag does not by itself establish the effective live setting.",
    "ordinaryOption": "A false secondary option clears trigger and enables scene query. For geometry kinds 4/5, simulation is cleared when actor-kind result is 2, or when concrete type word is 5 and its original body-flags getter lacks bit 0. Otherwise simulation is enabled. The named static implementation returns actor kind 0; the named dynamic implementation returns 1.",
    "bodyMode": "The original typed dynamic-body getter reads buffered or inline flags and clears bit 15. Bit 0 is consumed by mesh eligibility here; assigning its kinematic name also requires the matching API/setter evidence.",
    "finalSetter": "The computed byte is passed to the original shape setFlags interface. Successful return and any subsequent mutation remain separate from this offline branch proof."
  },
